From 33ca5445a17975c98b4e7800532bbf3de45c73af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hanoip <hanoip@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: add a legacy QSEECOM transport for
 HLOS-loaded TAs (hanoip FPC)

The FPC fingerprint TA on the Motorola Moto G60 (fpctzapp) is not
preloaded by the bootloader: Android loads it from the normal world with
QSEOS_APP_START_COMMAND and talks to it with 64-byte control blocks plus
one out-of-band data region. Its enrollment needs a hardware auth token
from the Gatekeeper inside the resident keymaster64, and the Gatekeeper
keeps its state in RPMB, which the TEE can only reach through the normal
world's listener service (RPMB_SERVICE 0x2000).

qcom_scm: add the legacy app management and send helpers this needs
(app_start/app_shutdown, physical-address send with and without the
whitelist sglist, app region notification) and the listener interface
(register via the smcinvoke variant, response with whitelist, deregister).
Calls that may return QSEOS_RESULT_INCOMPLETE use a variant without the
WARN_ON of qcom_scm_qseecom_call(): there the incomplete result is
expected and served by the caller.

qcom_qseecom_fpc: /dev/qseecom-fpc, a small transport (load, send, raw
send to a resident app, app id lookup). A listener is registered only for
the duration of one send and every INCOMPLETE is answered before the
deregistration; an idle registered listener makes the TEE wait forever and
the watchdog resets the board. The RPMB listener is served in-kernel
through the UFS RPMB W-LUN with the request/response layout of Qualcomm's
librpmb; authenticated writes are refused unless rpmb_writes=1 and
PROGRAM_KEY is always refused. region_phys defaults to 0: notifying
0x86d00000 hangs this board.

Protocol notes and validation: work/fingerprint-20261029/ in the
hanoip-mainline repository.
